8cdd4fd834ed0","cmd-812b627a6fbc4d90","cmd-c26b2d9c743c4d9f","cmd-1ba49510c07c457a","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has persistent 512 MiB zstd-compressed zram swap at maximum priority. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: it captures the original healthy boot, restart acknowledgement and connection loss, a different recovered boot identity, and restored node, service, and swap health; fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot change.","limitations":["No disk-backed swap was present for a side-by-side behavioral comparison; preference is established by the directly observed maximum zram swap priority.","The fixed lifecycle snapshots independently verify the reboot and general node hygiene but do not themselves inspect zram; recovered swap and service state comes from captured executor commands."]}
